# {{ .name }}

A Go CLI scaffolded by [guppy](https://nicedata.work/guppy) from the
`go-cli` template (extends `base-toolchain`).
{{ if .bazel }}
The dev environment is hermetic (Bazel + direnv, design §3.4):

```sh
direnv allow . # once per checkout — gup appears in .direnv/bin/ on cd
gup build         # bazel build //...
gup test          # bazel test //...
{{ if .linters }}gup lint          # bazel run //:gazelle -- -mode=diff (BUILD drift check)
{{ end }}```

No direnv? The same verbs work explicitly: `guppy project test`.

(A C compiler — gcc or clang — is the one system dependency rules_go's
cgo runtime needs; every versioned tool is pinned.)
{{ end }}
Or run the entrypoint directly:

```sh
go build -o {{ .name | kebab }} .
./{{ .name | kebab }} --greeting hi
```
